# Always open a PR

This project deploys from GitHub `main` to the VPS. Local-only fixes are not enough.

- After substantive code changes, **commit on a focused branch and open a PR** to `main` (do not leave work uncommitted/unpushed).
- Prefer small PRs with conventional commits (`fix`, `feat`, `chore`, …).
- Push with `-u` and create the PR via `gh pr create`; return the PR URL.
- Do not wait for the user to ask “make a PR” — shipping to VPS requires merge to `main`.
